(1, 2, 6, 'Mid term NN', 6, 100, 180, NULL, '{\"sections\": [{\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Requires extensive manual feature engineering\", \"Struggles with non-linear relationships\", \"Achieves higher accuracy on large datasets\", \"Limited to structured data types\"], \"question_text\": \"Which of the following is an advantage of deep learning over traditional machine learning in healthcare for patient readmission prediction?\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Multi-layered Neural Networks\", \"Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs)\", \"Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)\", \"Ensemble Deep Learning\"], \"question_text\": \"What type of neural network is best suited for handling temporal sequences of patient data?\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Final classification of the digit\", \"Detecting basic features like edges and curves\", \"Converting raw scores into probability distributions\", \"Receiving pixel values as input\"], \"question_text\": \"In a neural network for digit classification, what is the primary role of the first hidden layer?\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"The activation function to be used\", \"The strength of influence between neurons\", \"The number of hidden layers\", \"The learning rate of the network\"], \"question_text\": \"What does the \'weight function\' in a neural network determine?\", \"question_number\": 4}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"ReLU\", \"Sigmoid\", \"Tanh\", \"Softmax\"], \"question_text\": \"Which activation function is typically used in the output layer for digit classification to convert raw scores into probability distributions?\", \"question_number\": 5}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Decoder LSTM\", \"Attention Mechanism\", \"Encoder LSTM\", \"Output Layer\"], \"question_text\": \"For a real-time language translation app, which component of an LSTM-based Seq2Seq network processes the input language sentence?\", \"question_number\": 6}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Overfitting\", \"Vanishing gradient problem\", \"Computational overhead\", \"Lack of parallel processing\"], \"question_text\": \"What problem do LSTMs primarily solve that traditional RNNs struggle with, especially in long sequences?\", \"question_number\": 7}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Activation function\", \"Weight matrices\", \"Gating mechanisms\", \"Bias terms\"], \"question_text\": \"Which mechanism in an LSTM allows it to selectively retain or discard information?\", \"question_number\": 8}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Perfectly clean data\", \"Small datasets\", \"Missing data\", \"Low-dimensional data\"], \"question_text\": \"Deep learning models are generally more robust to which common issue in healthcare datasets?\", \"question_number\": 9}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Requires extensive manual feature engineering\", \"Automates feature learning\", \"Limited to pre-defined features\", \"Struggles with high-dimensional data\"], \"question_text\": \"What is a key advantage of deep learning in healthcare regarding feature engineering?\", \"question_number\": 10}], \"section_name\": \"Section A\", \"section_marks\": 20}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"List and briefly describe three application methods for deep learning in patient readmission prediction.\", \"question_number\": 11}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Explain how deep learning handles complex relationships and multimodal data integration, providing an advantage over traditional machine learning.\", \"question_number\": 12}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Describe the \'Forward Propagation Process\' in a neural network for digit classification, detailing the transformation of data through different layers.\", \"question_number\": 13}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Justify why LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Networks are recommended for a real-time language translation app, specifically referencing their data flow advantages.\", \"question_number\": 14}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Explain how LSTM\'s memory handling benefits, such as solving the vanishing gradient problem and selective memory, contribute to accurate language translation.\", \"question_number\": 15}], \"section_name\": \"Section B\", \"section_marks\": 25}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A healthcare startup wants to predict patient readmission risk. Discuss how deep learning can be applied in this scenario, detailing at least three application methods. Furthermore, elaborate on at least four advantages deep learning offers over traditional machine learning methods for this specific problem.\", \"question_number\": 16}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"You are designing a neural network to classify handwritten digits. Describe in detail how the network processes input from pixel data to output predictions. Your answer should include the role of the input layer, hidden layers (including how neurons compute output), connection weights, and the output layer. Explain the concept of hierarchical feature extraction.\", \"question_number\": 17}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A company wants to build a real-time language translation app. Recommend a suitable type of neural network architecture and provide a comprehensive justification for your choice. Your justification should explicitly reference data flow advantages (e.g., sequential processing, variable length handling) and memory handling benefits (e.g., long-term dependencies, selective memory) of the chosen architecture. Briefly mention an alternative and why your primary recommendation is preferable for real-time mobile applications.\", \"question_number\": 18}], \"section_name\": \"Section C\", \"section_marks\": 45}]}', 0, NULL, '2025-12-25 08:16:40'),
(2, 2, 6, 'cdghmgfd', 6, 100, 180, NULL, '{\"sections\": [{\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Natural Language Processing (NLP)\", \"options\": [\"Multi-layered Neural Networks\", \"Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs)\", \"Natural Language Processing (NLP)\", \"Ensemble Deep Learning\"], \"question_text\": \"Which deep learning approach is best suited for analyzing unstructured clinical notes and discharge summaries to extract biomedical concepts?\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Automatic Feature Learning\", \"options\": [\"Requires extensive manual feature engineering\", \"Struggles with non-linear relationships\", \"Automatic Feature Learning\", \"Limited to structured data types\"], \"question_text\": \"What is a key advantage of deep learning over traditional machine learning in handling medical data?\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Detects basic features like edges and curves\", \"options\": [\"Final classification\", \"Detects basic features like edges and curves\", \"Converts raw scores into probability distributions\", \"Receives pixel values directly\"], \"question_text\": \"In a neural network for digit classification, what is the primary role of the first hidden layer?\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"The strength of influence between neurons\", \"options\": [\"The number of layers\", \"The strength of influence between neurons\", \"The activation function type\", \"The input pixel values\"], \"question_text\": \"What does the \'weight function\' (connection weights) determine in a neural network?\", \"question_number\": 4}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Attention Mechanism\", \"options\": [\"Encoder LSTM\", \"Decoder LSTM\", \"Attention Mechanism\", \"Softmax activation\"], \"question_text\": \"Which component of an LSTM-based Seq2Seq network is responsible for focusing on relevant input parts during translation?\", \"question_number\": 5}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Vanishing gradient problem\", \"options\": [\"Overfitting\", \"Vanishing gradient problem\", \"Computational overhead\", \"Handling fixed-length inputs\"], \"question_text\": \"What problem do LSTMs primarily solve that traditional RNNs struggle with, especially in long sequences?\", \"question_number\": 6}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs)\", \"options\": [\"Multi-layered Neural Networks\", \"Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs)\", \"Natural Language Processing\", \"Ensemble Deep Learning\"], \"question_text\": \"Which deep learning method is specifically designed to handle temporal sequences of patient data?\", \"question_number\": 7}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"They are more robust to incomplete patient records.\", \"options\": [\"They require perfectly complete datasets.\", \"They are more robust to incomplete patient records.\", \"They automatically fill in missing values with averages.\", \"They cannot process data with any missing values.\"], \"question_text\": \"What is a benefit of deep learning models regarding missing data in healthcare settings?\", \"question_number\": 8}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Softmax activation\", \"options\": [\"ReLU activation\", \"Sigmoid activation\", \"Softmax activation\", \"Tanh activation\"], \"question_text\": \"In the forward propagation process for digit classification, what does the output layer typically use to convert raw scores into probability distributions?\", \"question_number\": 9}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Lower computational requirements and memory efficiency\", \"options\": [\"Superior performance on large datasets\", \"Lower computational requirements and memory efficiency\", \"Better at handling fixed-length inputs\", \"They do not require an attention mechanism\"], \"question_text\": \"Why are LSTMs considered preferable over Transformer architectures for real-time mobile language translation applications?\", \"question_number\": 10}], \"section_name\": \"Section A\", \"section_marks\": 20}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"A healthcare startup wants to predict patient readmission risk. Describe two specific application methods of deep learning for this scenario and briefly explain how each works.\", \"question_number\": 11}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Explain two advantages of deep learning over traditional machine learning methods when dealing with complex, high-dimensional medical data.\", \"question_number\": 12}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Describe the \'Layer-by-Layer Processing\' in a neural network designed for handwritten digit classification, focusing on the roles of hidden layers and how a neuron computes its output.\", \"question_number\": 13}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"For a real-time language translation app, explain why an LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) network is recommended, specifically highlighting its advantages in \'Data Flow\'.\", \"question_number\": 14}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Discuss two \'Memory Handling Benefits\' of LSTMs that make them suitable for processing long sequences in language translation.\", \"question_number\": 15}], \"section_name\": \"Section B\", \"section_marks\": 25}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A healthcare startup aims to predict patient readmission risk using historical data. Elaborate on how deep learning can be applied in this scenario, detailing at least three distinct application methods. Furthermore, discuss three key advantages deep learning offers over traditional machine learning approaches for this specific task.\", \"question_number\": 16}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"You are designing a neural network to classify handwritten digits from pixel data. Describe the entire process of how the network processes input from pixel data to output predictions. Your answer should include the role of the input layer, hidden layers (including how neurons compute output and the function of weights), and the output layer. Explain the concept of \'hierarchical feature extraction\' in this context.\", \"question_number\": 17}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A company wants to build a real-time language translation app. Recommend a suitable neural network architecture and provide a comprehensive justification for your choice. Your justification must explicitly reference \'Data Flow Advantages\' and \'Memory Handling Benefits\' of the chosen architecture. Additionally, briefly discuss why this architecture might be preferred over a more advanced alternative for real-time mobile deployment.\", \"question_number\": 18}], \"section_name\": \"Section C\", \"section_marks\": 45}], \"total_marks\": 100, \"duration_minutes\": 180}', 0, NULL, '2025-12-25 08:17:34'),
(3, 2, 7, 'mid term 22', 6, 100, 180, NULL, '{\"sections\": [{\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs)\", \"options\": [\"Multi-layered Neural Networks\", \"Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs)\", \"Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)\", \"Ensemble Deep Learning\"], \"question_text\": \"Which type of neural network is best suited for handling temporal sequences of patient data to capture how conditions evolve over time?\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Automatic Feature Learning\", \"options\": [\"Requires extensive manual feature engineering\", \"Struggles with non-linear relationships\", \"Automatic Feature Learning\", \"Limited to structured data types\"], \"question_text\": \"What is a key advantage of deep learning over traditional machine learning in healthcare for patient readmission prediction?\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Detects basic features like edges and curves\", \"options\": [\"Final classification of digits\", \"Detects basic features like edges and curves\", \"Converts raw scores into probability distributions\", \"Receives pixel values directly\"], \"question_text\": \"In a neural network for digit classification, what is the primary role of the first hidden layer?\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"The strength of influence between neurons in consecutive layers\", \"options\": [\"The number of layers in the network\", \"The strength of influence between neurons in consecutive layers\", \"The activation function used by neurons\", \"The learning rate of the network\"], \"question_text\": \"What do connection weights determine in a neural network?\", \"question_number\": 4}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Softmax\", \"options\": [\"ReLU\", \"Sigmoid\", \"Tanh\", \"Softmax\"], \"question_text\": \"Which activation function is typically used in the output layer for multi-class classification problems like digit recognition to convert raw scores into probability distributions?\", \"question_number\": 5}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Attention Mechanism\", \"options\": [\"Encoder LSTM\", \"Decoder LSTM\", \"Attention Mechanism\", \"Input Layer\"], \"question_text\": \"For a real-time language translation app, which component of an LSTM-based Seq2Seq network is responsible for focusing on relevant input parts during translation?\", \"question_number\": 6}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Vanishing gradient problem\", \"options\": [\"Overfitting\", \"Vanishing gradient problem\", \"Exploding gradient problem\", \"Computational overhead\"], \"question_text\": \"What problem do LSTMs primarily solve that traditional RNNs struggle with, especially in long sequences?\", \"question_number\": 7}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Lower computational requirements and memory efficiency\", \"options\": [\"Better handling of variable length sequences\", \"Lower computational requirements and memory efficiency\", \"Superior long-term dependency capture\", \"Faster convergence rates\"], \"question_text\": \"Why are LSTMs often preferred over Transformer architectures for real-time mobile applications, despite Transformers offering superior performance?\", \"question_number\": 8}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Unstructured clinical notes and discharge summaries\", \"options\": [\"Vital signs and lab results\", \"Patient demographics\", \"Unstructured clinical notes and discharge summaries\", \"Medical history only\"], \"question_text\": \"What kind of data can Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques analyze in the context of patient readmission prediction?\", \"question_number\": 9}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"answer\": \"Hierarchical feature extraction leading to abstract representations\", \"options\": [\"Random noise\", \"Hierarchical feature extraction leading to abstract representations\", \"Only numerical values\", \"Direct digit classifications without intermediate steps\"], \"question_text\": \"In the forward propagation process for digit classification, what does the network transform low-level pixel data into?\", \"question_number\": 10}], \"section_name\": \"Section A\", \"section_marks\": 20}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"A healthcare startup wants to predict patient readmission risk. Describe two specific deep learning application methods that can be used and briefly explain how each contributes to the prediction.\", \"question_number\": 11}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Explain the concept of \'Automatic Feature Learning\' in deep learning and why it is particularly advantageous in the context of medical data for patient readmission prediction.\", \"question_number\": 12}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Describe the information flow in a neural network designed for handwritten digit classification, from input pixels to the final output layer. Mention the role of different layers.\", \"question_number\": 13}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"When designing a neural network, how are \'connection weights\' adjusted during the learning process, and what is their ultimate purpose in pattern recognition?\", \"question_number\": 14}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Explain how LSTM\'s gating mechanisms (forget, input, output gates) contribute to its \'selective memory\' and \'context preservation\' capabilities, which are crucial for language translation.\", \"question_number\": 15}], \"section_name\": \"Section B\", \"section_marks\": 25}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A healthcare startup aims to predict patient readmission risk. Discuss in detail how deep learning can be applied in this scenario, outlining at least three distinct application methods. Furthermore, elaborate on at least three significant advantages deep learning offers over traditional machine learning approaches for this specific problem.\", \"question_number\": 16}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"You are designing a neural network to classify handwritten digits. Describe the network\'s architecture and the step-by-step process of how it transforms raw pixel data into a digit prediction. Your answer should clearly explain the role of the input layer, hidden layers (including how neurons compute output), connection weights, and the final output layer, detailing how each contributes to hierarchical feature extraction and classification.\", \"question_number\": 17}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A company wants to build a real-time language translation app. Recommend the most suitable type of neural network architecture for this task, justifying your choice comprehensively. Your justification should include a detailed discussion of its data flow advantages (e.g., sequential processing, variable length handling) and memory handling benefits (e.g., long-term dependencies, selective memory). Also, briefly compare its suitability for real-time mobile deployment against an alternative advanced architecture.\", \"question_number\": 18}], \"section_name\": \"Section C\", \"section_marks\": 45}], \"total_marks\": 100, \"duration_minutes\": 180}', 0, NULL, '2026-01-04 09:26:20'),
(4, 2, 2, 'Test Question Paper', NULL, 50, 120, NULL, '{\"sections\": [{\"type\": \"Multiple Choice\", \"questions\": [{\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [{\"id\": \"a\", \"text\": \"To define a block of reusable code.\"}, {\"id\": \"b\", \"text\": \"To store and manage data values.\"}, {\"id\": \"c\", \"text\": \"To repeat a set of instructions multiple times.\"}, {\"id\": \"d\", \"text\": \"To group multiple values of different types.\"}], \"question_text\": \"What is the primary purpose of a variable in programming?\", \"correct_answer\": \"b\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [{\"id\": \"a\", \"text\": \"Storing a collection of similar data types.\"}, {\"id\": \"b\", \"text\": \"Repeating a block of code for a specified number of times.\"}, {\"id\": \"c\", \"text\": \"Encapsulating a specific operation or task.\"}, {\"id\": \"d\", \"text\": \"Declaring a named memory location for data.\"}], \"question_text\": \"Which of the following best describes what a function performs?\", \"correct_answer\": \"c\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [{\"id\": \"a\", \"text\": \"To declare a new data type.\"}, {\"id\": \"b\", \"text\": \"To execute a block of code repeatedly.\"}, {\"id\": \"c\", \"text\": \"To store multiple values under a single name.\"}, {\"id\": \"d\", \"text\": \"To define a set of instructions for a specific task.\"}], \"question_text\": \"What is the main utility of a loop in programming?\", \"correct_answer\": \"b\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [{\"id\": \"a\", \"text\": \"To perform complex mathematical calculations.\"}, {\"id\": \"b\", \"text\": \"To store a single value that can change.\"}, {\"id\": \"c\", \"text\": \"To hold multiple values of the same type in an ordered collection.\"}, {\"id\": \"d\", \"text\": \"To define a subroutine that can be called by name.\"}], \"question_text\": \"In computer science, what is an array primarily used for?\", \"correct_answer\": \"c\", \"question_number\": 4}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [{\"id\": \"a\", \"text\": \"A variable\"}, {\"id\": \"b\", \"text\": \"A function\"}, {\"id\": \"c\", \"text\": \"A loop\"}, {\"id\": \"d\", \"text\": \"An array\"}], \"question_text\": \"If you need to process a list of 100 student scores, which programming construct would be most efficient for iterating through each score?\", \"correct_answer\": \"c\", \"question_number\": 5}], \"instructions\": \"Answer all 5 questions. Each question carries 2 marks. Choose the best option.\", \"section_name\": \"Section A\", \"marks_per_question\": 2}, {\"type\": \"Short Answer\", \"questions\": [{\"type\": \"short_answer\", \"marks\": 20, \"question_text\": \"Explain the concepts of \'variables\' and \'arrays\' in programming. Describe their fundamental differences and provide a practical scenario where using an array would be significantly more advantageous than using individual variables.\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"short_answer\", \"marks\": 20, \"question_text\": \"Discuss the roles of \'functions\' and \'loops\' in structuring and optimizing code. Provide an example of a common programming task (e.g., calculating the average of a list of numbers, processing items in a shopping cart) where both a function and a loop would be essential components, explaining how each contributes to the solution.\", \"question_number\": 2}], \"instructions\": \"Answer all 2 questions. Each question carries 20 marks. Provide detailed explanations.\", \"section_name\": \"Section B\", \"marks_per_question\": 20}], \"exam_title\": \"Computer Science Fundamentals\", \"total_marks\": 50, \"total_time_minutes\": 120}', 0, NULL, '2026-01-04 09:41:43'),
(5, 2, 7, 'endo termo', 6, 100, 180, NULL, '{\"sections\": [{\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Requires extensive manual feature engineering\", \"Struggles with non-linear relationships\", \"Automatic feature learning\", \"Limited to structured data\"], \"question_text\": \"Which of the following is an advantage of deep learning over traditional machine learning for patient readmission prediction?\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)\", \"Recurrent Neural Network (RNN)\", \"Multilayer Perceptron (MLP)\", \"Autoencoder\"], \"question_text\": \"What type of neural network is best suited for handling temporal sequences of patient data?\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"To perform activation functions\", \"To receive pixel values as features\", \"To combine complex patterns\", \"To output final probabilities\"], \"question_text\": \"In a neural network for digit classification, what is the primary role of the input layer?\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"The bias of the neuron\", \"The strength of influence between neurons\", \"The activation function\", \"The learning rate\"], \"question_text\": \"What does the \'weight\' in a neural network connection represent?\", \"question_number\": 4}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"ReLU\", \"Sigmoid\", \"Tanh\", \"Softmax\"], \"question_text\": \"Which activation function is commonly used in the output layer of a multi-class classification problem to convert raw scores into probability distributions?\", \"question_number\": 5}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Overfitting\", \"Vanishing/Exploding Gradients\", \"Computational complexity\", \"Lack of parallelization\"], \"question_text\": \"What problem do LSTMs primarily address that traditional RNNs struggle with?\", \"question_number\": 6}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Input layer\", \"Output layer\", \"Gating mechanisms\", \"Activation function\"], \"question_text\": \"Which component of an LSTM allows it to selectively retain or discard information?\", \"question_number\": 7}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Decoder LSTM\", \"Encoder LSTM\", \"Attention Mechanism\", \"Output Layer\"], \"question_text\": \"For a real-time language translation app, which part of an LSTM-based Seq2Seq model processes the input language sentence?\", \"question_number\": 8}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"They always output negative values.\", \"They cause exploding gradients.\", \"They suffer from vanishing gradients and saturation.\", \"They are computationally expensive.\"], \"question_text\": \"Why might sigmoid activation functions lead to poor performance in deep networks?\", \"question_number\": 9}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"It requires separate models for each data type.\", \"It struggles with diverse data types simultaneously.\", \"It can effectively process diverse data types simultaneously.\", \"It only works with numerical data.\"], \"question_text\": \"What is a key advantage of deep learning in integrating multimodal data (e.g., structured data, text, temporal sequences)?\", \"question_number\": 10}], \"section_name\": \"Section A\"}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 7, \"question_text\": \"A student uses sigmoid activation function in all layers of a deep network and notices poor performance. Explain why this might be happening and suggest an alternative activation function, justifying your choice.\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 7, \"question_text\": \"Explain the concept of \'vanishing gradients\' in deep neural networks and how it impacts model training.\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 7, \"question_text\": \"Differentiate between feedforward neural networks and recurrent neural networks, highlighting their primary applications.\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 7, \"question_text\": \"What is the purpose of an \'attention mechanism\' in sequence-to-sequence models? Provide a brief example of its utility.\", \"question_number\": 4}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 7, \"question_text\": \"Describe the role of \'bias\' in a neural network neuron. How does it affect the neuron\'s output?\", \"question_number\": 5}], \"section_name\": \"Section B\"}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A healthcare startup wants to predict patient readmission risk using historical data. How can deep learning be applied in this scenario? What advantages does it offer over traditional machine learning?\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"You\'re designing a neural network to classify handwritten digits. Describe how the network processes input from pixel data to output predictions. Include the role of layers and weights.\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A company wants to build a real-time language translation app. Which type of neural network would you recommend and why? Justify your choice with reference to data flow and memory handling.\", \"question_number\": 3}], \"section_name\": \"Section C\"}], \"total_marks\": 100, \"duration_minutes\": 180}', 0, NULL, '2026-01-04 09:45:45'),
(6, 2, 2, 'Debug Test Paper', NULL, 50, 120, NULL, '{\"sections\": [{\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Queue\", \"Stack\", \"Linked List\", \"Array\"], \"question_text\": \"Which of the following data structures operates on the principle of Last-In, First-Out (LIFO)?\", \"correct_answer\": \"Stack\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Inheritance\", \"Polymorphism\", \"Encapsulation\", \"Abstraction\"], \"question_text\": \"In Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), what concept refers to the bundling of data and methods that operate on the data within a single unit?\", \"correct_answer\": \"Encapsulation\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"If-else statement\", \"While loop\", \"Do-while loop\", \"For loop\"], \"question_text\": \"Which control structure is best suited for executing a block of code a specific, predetermined number of times?\", \"correct_answer\": \"For loop\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"It is a fixed value that cannot change.\", \"It is a named storage location for data that can be modified.\", \"It defines a block of code that performs a specific task.\", \"It is a condition that evaluates to true or false.\"], \"question_text\": \"What is the primary characteristic of a \'variable\' in programming?\", \"correct_answer\": \"It is a named storage location for data that can be modified.\", \"question_number\": 4}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Integer\", \"Boolean\", \"Float\", \"String\"], \"question_text\": \"Which of these data types is typically used to store a sequence of characters?\", \"correct_answer\": \"String\", \"question_number\": 5}], \"section_name\": \"Section A\"}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 10, \"question_text\": \"Explain the difference between \'pass by value\' and \'pass by reference\' in function calls. Provide a simple pseudo-code example for each to illustrate how parameters are handled.\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 10, \"question_text\": \"Describe the four main principles of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP): Encapsulation, Inheritance, Polymorphism, and Abstraction. For each principle, provide a brief explanation and a real-world or programming example.\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 10, \"question_text\": \"Compare and contrast Arrays and Linked Lists as fundamental data structures. Discuss their advantages, disadvantages, and typical use cases where one might be preferred over the other.\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 10, \"question_text\": \"Explain the concept of recursion in programming. Provide a pseudo-code example of a recursive function to calculate the factorial of a number. Discuss potential advantages and disadvantages of using recursion.\", \"question_number\": 4}], \"section_name\": \"Section B\"}], \"total_marks\": 50, \"duration_minutes\": 120}', 0, NULL, '2026-01-04 09:51:33'),
(7, 2, 6, 'uygyug', 6, 100, 180, NULL, '{\"sections\": [{\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Multi-layered Neural Networks\", \"Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs)\", \"Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)\", \"Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs)\"], \"question_text\": \"What type of neural network is best suited for handling temporal sequences of patient data to predict readmission risk?\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Requires extensive manual feature engineering\", \"Limited to linear relationships\", \"Automatically discovers complex patterns without manual feature engineering\", \"Struggles with high-dimensional medical data\"], \"question_text\": \"Which advantage does deep learning offer over traditional machine learning in healthcare, particularly regarding feature engineering?\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"To detect edges and curves\", \"To compute activation functions\", \"To receive pixel values representing grayscale intensities\", \"To output the final digit prediction\"], \"question_text\": \"In a neural network for digit classification, what is the primary role of the input layer?\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"The type of activation function\", \"The strength of influence between neurons in consecutive layers\", \"The number of hidden layers\", \"The learning rate of the network\"], \"question_text\": \"What do connection weights determine in a neural network?\", \"question_number\": 4}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"ReLU\", \"Sigmoid\", \"Tanh\", \"Softmax\"], \"question_text\": \"Which activation function is typically used in the output layer of a digit classification network to convert raw scores into probability distributions?\", \"question_number\": 5}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Encoder LSTM\", \"Decoder LSTM\", \"Attention Mechanism\", \"Cell State\"], \"question_text\": \"For a real-time language translation app, which component of an LSTM-based Seq2Seq network is responsible for focusing on relevant input parts during translation?\", \"question_number\": 6}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Overfitting\", \"Vanishing gradient problem\", \"Exploding gradient problem\", \"Computational overhead\"], \"question_text\": \"What problem do LSTMs primarily solve that traditional RNNs struggle with, especially in long sequences?\", \"question_number\": 7}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Multi-layered Neural Networks\", \"Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs)\", \"Natural Language Processing (NLP)\", \"Ensemble Deep Learning\"], \"question_text\": \"Which deep learning application method would be used to analyze unstructured clinical notes and discharge summaries to extract relevant biomedical concepts?\", \"question_number\": 8}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Limited data is available\", \"Sufficient data is available\", \"Only structured data is used\", \"Manual feature engineering is applied\"], \"question_text\": \"Deep learning models are generally shown to achieve higher accuracy compared to traditional methods when what condition is met?\", \"question_number\": 9}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"options\": [\"Raw pixel values\", \"Simple features into complex patterns\", \"Probability distributions\", \"Output layer scores\"], \"question_text\": \"In the context of a neural network for digit classification, what do deeper hidden layers typically combine?\", \"question_number\": 10}], \"instructions\": \"Answer all questions. Each question carries 2 marks.\", \"section_name\": \"Section A\"}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 7, \"question_text\": \"List and briefly describe three advantages of deep learning over traditional machine learning in the context of patient readmission risk prediction.\", \"question_number\": 11}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 7, \"question_text\": \"Briefly describe the role of connection weights and bias in a neuron\'s computation within a neural network, as described by the formula: output = activation((weight * input) + bias).\", \"question_number\": 12}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 7, \"question_text\": \"Explain how an LSTM network addresses and solves the \'vanishing gradient problem\' to handle long-term dependencies in sequential data.\", \"question_number\": 13}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 7, \"question_text\": \"What are the three main components of an LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) architecture recommended for real-time language translation, and what is the primary function of each?\", \"question_number\": 14}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 7, \"question_text\": \"Describe the information flow within a neural network for digit classification, explaining how low-level pixel data is transformed through hierarchical feature extraction to ultimately map visual patterns to digit classifications.\", \"question_number\": 15}], \"instructions\": \"Answer all questions. Each question carries 7 marks.\", \"section_name\": \"Section B\"}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A healthcare startup aims to predict patient readmission risk using historical data. Discuss in detail how deep learning can be applied in this scenario, outlining at least three specific application methods. Furthermore, elaborate on at least four significant advantages deep learning offers over traditional machine learning approaches for this task.\", \"question_number\": 16}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"Describe the complete process of how a neural network classifies handwritten digits, starting from the input of pixel data to the final output prediction. Your answer should clearly explain the role of different layers (input, hidden, output) and how connection weights contribute to the learning and processing through forward propagation.\", \"question_number\": 17}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A company plans to develop a real-time language translation application for mobile devices. Recommend a suitable neural network architecture, justifying your choice by detailing its data flow advantages (e.g., sequential processing, variable length handling) and memory handling benefits (e.g., long-term dependencies, selective memory). Also, briefly discuss why this architecture might be preferred over more advanced alternatives like Transformer models for real-time mobile deployment.\", \"question_number\": 18}], \"instructions\": \"Answer all questions. Each question carries 15 marks.\", \"section_name\": \"Section C\"}], \"total_marks\": 100, \"duration_minutes\": 180}', 0, NULL, '2026-01-04 11:30:42'),
(8, 2, 6, 'Neural Network', 6, 100, 180, NULL, '{\"sections\": [{\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 3, \"question_text\": \"Which deep learning approach is specifically designed to handle temporal sequences of patient data, capturing how conditions evolve over time?\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 3, \"question_text\": \"What key advantage does deep learning offer in processing medical data by automatically identifying complex patterns without manual feature engineering?\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 3, \"question_text\": \"Which deep learning technique is most suitable for analyzing unstructured clinical notes and discharge summaries to extract relevant biomedical concepts?\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 3, \"question_text\": \"When integrating diverse data types like structured lab values, unstructured text, and temporal sequences, what is a significant benefit of deep learning?\", \"question_number\": 4}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 3, \"question_text\": \"In the context of patient readmission prediction, deep learning models generally achieve superior performance compared to traditional methods when what condition is met?\", \"question_number\": 5}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 3, \"question_text\": \"For a neural network classifying handwritten digits, what information does the input layer primarily receive?\", \"question_number\": 6}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 3, \"question_text\": \"What is the fundamental role of connection weights between neurons in consecutive layers of a neural network?\", \"question_number\": 7}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 3, \"question_text\": \"Which activation function is typically used in the output layer of a multi-class classification neural network to convert raw scores into probability distributions?\", \"question_number\": 8}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 3, \"question_text\": \"For a real-time language translation application requiring the handling of sequential data and long-term dependencies, which neural network architecture is most recommended?\", \"question_number\": 9}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 3, \"question_text\": \"In an LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence model for translation, what mechanism helps the decoder focus on relevant parts of the input sentence?\", \"question_number\": 10}], \"section_name\": \"Section A\"}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Briefly describe two distinct methods by which deep learning can be applied to predict patient readmission risk.\", \"question_number\": 11}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"List and briefly explain two advantages of using deep learning over traditional machine learning for analyzing complex healthcare data.\", \"question_number\": 12}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Explain the hierarchical feature extraction process within the hidden layers of a neural network designed for handwritten digit classification.\", \"question_number\": 13}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Describe how connection weights are adjusted during the training phase of a neural network and their significance in pattern recognition.\", \"question_number\": 14}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Justify why Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks are particularly effective in handling long-term dependencies and solving the vanishing gradient problem, making them suitable for language translation tasks.\", \"question_number\": 15}], \"section_name\": \"Section B\"}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A healthcare startup aims to develop a system for predicting patient readmission risk using a vast amount of historical data. Discuss in detail the various ways deep learning can be applied in this scenario, outlining specific architectural approaches. Furthermore, elaborate on the key advantages deep learning offers over traditional machine learning methods for this particular task.\", \"question_number\": 16}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"You are tasked with designing a neural network to classify handwritten digits from pixel data. Provide a comprehensive description of how this network processes input, from the initial pixel data to the final output prediction. Your explanation must clearly detail the role of different layers (input, hidden, output), the function and adjustment of connection weights, and the overall flow of information during forward propagation.\", \"question_number\": 17}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"A company intends to build a real-time language translation application. Recommend a specific type of neural network architecture that would be most suitable for this purpose. Justify your recommendation thoroughly by discussing its advantages concerning data flow, its ability to handle memory and long-term dependencies, and its implications for real-time performance. Also, briefly mention any alternative architectures and why your chosen one might be preferred in a real-time mobile context.\", \"question_number\": 18}], \"section_name\": \"Section C\"}]}', 1, '2026-01-05 14:21:50', '2026-01-05 19:51:10'),
(9, 2, 5, 'AI question paper ', 4, 100, 180, NULL, '{\"sections\": [{\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"question_text\": \"What is the primary purpose of using sentiment analysis in the AI-driven market research phase?\", \"question_number\": 1}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"question_text\": \"Which AI-driven technique is explicitly mentioned for developing detailed customer personas?\", \"question_number\": 2}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"question_text\": \"In the context of AI-enhanced product development, what does \'AI-driven feature prioritization\' primarily rely on?\", \"question_number\": 3}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"question_text\": \"Which of the following is NOT a component of the \'Place Strategy\' in the AI-powered marketing mix optimization?\", \"question_number\": 4}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"question_text\": \"What is a key consideration for \'Bias prevention\' in the Ethical AI Marketing Framework?\", \"question_number\": 5}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"question_text\": \"The project requires challenging an established product in the online marketplace. What is the role of the student in this scenario?\", \"question_number\": 6}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"question_text\": \"Which deliverable focuses on mapping the complete customer journey from awareness to advocacy?\", \"question_number\": 7}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"question_text\": \"What type of AI platform is specifically mentioned for analyzing competitor products and identifying market opportunities?\", \"question_number\": 8}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"question_text\": \"Which of the following is a component of the \'Promotion Strategy\' with AI integration?\", \"question_number\": 9}, {\"type\": \"mcq\", \"marks\": 2, \"question_text\": \"What is one of the primary learning objectives related to ethical AI frameworks?\", \"question_number\": 10}], \"section_name\": \"Section A\"}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Briefly explain how AI tools can be utilized to conduct a comprehensive competitive analysis and identify market gaps for a new product.\", \"question_number\": 11}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Describe the key components of \'Customer Journey Mapping and Persona Development\' using AI-assisted techniques, as outlined in the project context.\", \"question_number\": 12}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Outline the three levels of personalization (standardization, personalization, hyper-personalization) that need to be considered when developing a brand equity building strategy with AI insights.\", \"question_number\": 13}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"Explain how AI can enhance the \'Pricing Strategy\' within the marketing mix optimization phase.\", \"question_number\": 14}, {\"type\": \"short\", \"marks\": 5, \"question_text\": \"List and briefly describe three critical aspects that must be addressed in an \'Ethical AI Marketing Framework\'.\", \"question_number\": 15}], \"section_name\": \"Section B\"}, {\"questions\": [{\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"You are tasked with developing a \'New Product Concept\' for a competing product. Detail how AI can be practically applied across the entire process, from identifying unique value propositions to developing brand identity. Provide specific examples for each step.\", \"question_number\": 16}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"Elaborate on the \'AI-Powered Marketing Mix Optimization\' (4Ps) phase. For each of the 4Ps (Product, Pricing, Promotion, Place), explain how AI integration can lead to strategic advantages and provide specific examples of AI applications.\", \"question_number\": 17}, {\"type\": \"long\", \"marks\": 15, \"question_text\": \"Discuss the importance of the \'Implementation Roadmap and Ethical Framework\' in the context of launching an AI-powered marketing strategy. Explain how the deliverables in this phase ensure a successful and responsible market entry.\", \"question_number\": 18}], \"section_name\": \"Section C\"}]}', 1, '2026-01-06 01:28:10', '2026-01-06 06:57:55');

-- --------------------------------------------------------

--
-- Table structure for table `ai_quizzes`
--

CREATE TABLE `ai_quizzes` (
  `id` int NOT NULL,
  `user_id` int NOT NULL,
  `resource_id` int DEFAULT NULL,
  `subject_id` int DEFAULT NULL,
  `title` varchar(200) NOT NULL,
  `difficulty` enum('easy','medium','hard') DEFAULT 'medium',
  `num_questions` int DEFAULT '10',
  `quiz_data` json DEFAULT NULL,
  `is_published` tinyint(1) DEFAULT '0',
  `published_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  `created_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;

--
-- Dumping data for table `ai_quizzes`
--

INSERT INTO `ai_quizzes` (`id`, `user_id`, `resource_id`, `subject_id`, `title`, `difficulty`, `num_questions`, `quiz_data`, `is_published`, `published_at`, `created_at`) VALUES
(3, 2, 2, NULL, '123', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Asymmetric Key Cryptography\", \"B) Symmetric Key Cryptography\", \"C) Hashing Algorithm\", \"D) Digital Signatures\"], \"question\": \"Which cryptographic technique ensures the confidentiality of files during transmission by using the same key for both encryption and decryption?\", \"explanation\": \"Symmetric Key Cryptography uses a single, shared key for both encrypting and decrypting data, making it suitable for ensuring confidentiality when the key can be securely exchanged.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To encrypt transactions for privacy.\", \"B) To create a unique, fixed-size fingerprint of data for integrity verification.\", \"C) To establish a secure communication channel between nodes.\", \"D) To digitally sign transactions for authentication.\"], \"question\": \"What is the primary purpose of a hashing algorithm in a blockchain network?\", \"explanation\": \"Hashing algorithms generate a unique, fixed-size output (hash) from input data. In blockchain, this hash is used to link blocks and ensure the integrity of the data within each block, as any change to the data would result in a different hash.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) The ability to quickly modify past transactions.\", \"B) The property that once data is recorded on the blockchain, it cannot be altered or deleted.\", \"C) The process of reaching agreement among network participants.\", \"D) The capacity to scale the network to accommodate more users.\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following best describes the immutability feature of a blockchain network?\", \"explanation\": \"Immutability in blockchain refers to the characteristic that once a transaction or block of data is added to the chain, it becomes a permanent and unchangeable record, secured by cryptographic links and consensus mechanisms.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Immediately upon project assignment.\", \"B) Only after the client confirms project completion based on agreed terms.\", \"C) When the freelancer requests an advance payment.\", \"D) After a fixed period, regardless of project status.\"], \"question\": \"In a smart contract scenario for a freelancing platform, when are funds typically released to the freelancer?\", \"explanation\": \"Smart contracts are self-executing agreements. In a freelancing scenario, the contract is programmed to release funds only when predefined conditions are met, such as the client\'s confirmation of project completion, ensuring payments are tied to deliverables.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Ensuring fast transaction processing speeds.\", \"B) Achieving consensus among potentially untrustworthy or faulty nodes.\", \"C) Managing large volumes of data storage.\", \"D) Preventing unauthorized access to private keys.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main challenge addressed by the Byzantine General Problem in distributed systems like blockchain?\", \"explanation\": \"The Byzantine General Problem illustrates the difficulty of achieving consensus in a distributed system where some participants (generals) may be unreliable or malicious. Byzantine Fault Tolerance (BFT) mechanisms are designed to overcome this challenge and ensure agreement even with faulty nodes.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}]}', 0, NULL, '2025-12-18 09:36:21'),
(4, 2, 2, NULL, 'quiz3', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Asymmetric Cipher Model\", \"B) Symmetric Cipher Model\", \"C) Hashing Algorithm\", \"D) Digital Signature\"], \"question\": \"Based on the scenario where a software company sends confidential files using the same encryption key for both encryption and decryption, which cryptographic model is being used?\", \"explanation\": \"The scenario explicitly states \'Both locations use the same encryption key to encrypt and decrypt files,\' which is the defining characteristic of a symmetric cipher model.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To encrypt transactions for privacy.\", \"B) To create digital signatures for authentication.\", \"C) To link blocks together and ensure data integrity.\", \"D) To generate new cryptocurrencies.\"], \"question\": \"What is the primary use of a hashing algorithm in blockchain technology?\", \"explanation\": \"Hashing algorithms generate a unique fixed-size output for input data. In blockchain, each block contains the hash of the previous block, creating an immutable chain and ensuring data integrity.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Distributed Ledger\", \"B) Consensus Mechanism\", \"C) Centralized Server\", \"D) Cryptography\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is NOT considered a core component of blockchain architecture?\", \"explanation\": \"Blockchain is fundamentally decentralized, relying on a distributed ledger, consensus mechanisms, and cryptography, rather than a centralized server.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) By manually verifying client satisfaction.\", \"B) By automatically executing payment upon a predefined condition (client confirmation).\", \"C) By requiring a third-party arbitrator for every transaction.\", \"D) By encrypting the payment details until completion.\"], \"question\": \"In a freelancing platform scenario where funds are released only after the client confirms project completion, how do smart contracts primarily ensure payment is tied to deliverables?\", \"explanation\": \"Smart contracts are self-executing agreements where the terms are directly written into code. In this scenario, the contract is programmed to release funds automatically once the condition of \'client confirmation of project completion\' is met.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) The ability to easily modify past transactions.\", \"B) The resistance of recorded data to alteration or deletion.\", \"C) The speed at which new blocks are added to the chain.\", \"D) The privacy of transaction details.\"], \"question\": \"What does the term \'immutability\' signify in a blockchain network?\", \"explanation\": \"Immutability in blockchain means that once data (transactions) is recorded on the blockchain and a block is added, it cannot be changed or deleted, ensuring a permanent and tamper-proof record.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To create new Bitcoin wallets.\", \"B) To validate transactions and add new blocks to the blockchain.\", \"C) To exchange Bitcoin for other cryptocurrencies.\", \"D) To encrypt user data for privacy.\"], \"question\": \"What is the primary purpose of \'mining\' in the Bitcoin network?\", \"explanation\": \"Bitcoin mining involves solving complex computational puzzles to validate pending transactions and bundle them into new blocks, which are then added to the blockchain, thereby securing the network and creating new bitcoins.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) It uses a Proof of Work consensus mechanism.\", \"B) It supports smart contracts and decentralized applications (DApps).\", \"C) It has a fixed supply of its native cryptocurrency.\", \"D) Its primary purpose is to be a digital currency for transactions.\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is a key feature that distinguishes Ethereum from Bitcoin?\", \"explanation\": \"While Bitcoin is primarily a digital currency, Ethereum was designed to be a platform for smart contracts and DApps, allowing developers to build and deploy decentralized applications.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Ensuring high transaction speed.\", \"B) Achieving consensus among untrustworthy or failing nodes.\", \"C) Managing centralized database integrity.\", \"D) Reducing energy consumption.\"], \"question\": \"The Byzantine General Problem illustrates a challenge in distributed systems related to:\", \"explanation\": \"The Byzantine General Problem describes the difficulty of achieving consensus in a distributed system where some components (generals/nodes) may be unreliable or malicious, leading to the concept of Byzantine Fault Tolerance (BFT) in blockchain.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Proof of Work (PoW)\", \"B) Proof of Stake (PoS)\", \"C) Proof of Burn (PoB)\", \"D) Proof of Centralization (PoCen)\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is NOT a common consensus algorithm used in blockchain networks?\", \"explanation\": \"Proof of Work, Proof of Stake, and Proof of Burn are all established consensus algorithms. \'Proof of Centralization\' is not a recognized consensus algorithm in blockchain, as blockchain aims for decentralization.\", \"correct_answer\": \"D\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) By centralizing all land records in a single government database.\", \"B) By making land records immutable, transparent, and resistant to fraud.\", \"C) By eliminating the need for any legal documentation.\", \"D) By speeding up physical property inspections.\"], \"question\": \"How can Distributed Ledger Technology (DLT) significantly improve the process of Land Registration?\", \"explanation\": \"DLT, like blockchain, can create a tamper-proof, transparent, and decentralized record of land ownership, reducing fraud, disputes, and bureaucratic inefficiencies by making records immutable and accessible to authorized parties.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}]}', 0, NULL, '2025-12-18 10:45:21'),
(5, 2, 6, NULL, 'NN quiz', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) By using multi-layered neural networks to process complex patient data\", \"B) By employing Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs) to handle temporal sequences of patient data\", \"C) By utilizing Natural Language Processing (NLP) to analyze unstructured clinical notes\", \"D) All of the above\"], \"question\": \"How can deep learning be applied to predict patient readmission risk in a healthcare startup scenario?\", \"explanation\": \"Deep learning offers multiple approaches including multi-layered NNs for complex data, RNNs for temporal data, and NLP for unstructured text, all contributing to patient readmission prediction.\", \"correct_answer\": \"D\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) It requires extensive manual feature engineering\", \"B) It struggles with non-linear relationships between variables\", \"C) It automatically discovers complex patterns and interactions without manual feature engineering\", \"D) It performs poorly on large datasets\"], \"question\": \"What is a significant advantage of deep learning over traditional machine learning methods when predicting patient readmission risk, especially given the high-dimensional nature of medical data?\", \"explanation\": \"Deep learning\'s automatic feature learning capability is a key advantage, as it eliminates the need for manual feature engineering, which is particularly valuable in high-dimensional medical datasets.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Multi-layered Neural Networks\", \"B) Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs)\", \"C) Natural Language Processing (NLP)\", \"D) Ensemble Deep Learning\"], \"question\": \"Which deep learning approach is specifically designed to analyze unstructured clinical notes and discharge summaries to extract relevant biomedical concepts for patient readmission prediction?\", \"explanation\": \"Natural Language Processing (NLP) is the deep learning technique specifically used to analyze and extract information from unstructured text data like clinical notes and discharge summaries.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) When data is scarce and limited\", \"B) When only highly structured data is available\", \"C) When sufficient data is available for training\", \"D) When manual feature engineering is the primary method\"], \"question\": \"Under which condition do deep learning models typically achieve higher accuracy, recall, and AUC compared to traditional machine learning methods in healthcare applications?\", \"explanation\": \"Research indicates that deep learning models achieve superior performance metrics (accuracy, recall, AUC) when sufficient data is available for training, as they can learn more complex patterns.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To receive the raw pixel values as input\", \"B) To perform the final classification of the digit\", \"C) To detect basic features like edges, curves, and orientations\", \"D) To combine simple features into complex patterns like loops and intersections\"], \"question\": \"In a neural network designed to classify handwritten digits, what is the primary role of the first hidden layer during the forward propagation process?\", \"explanation\": \"The first hidden layer in a digit classification network is typically responsible for detecting basic, low-level features such as edges, curves, and orientations from the raw pixel data.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) They are randomly assigned and remain constant\", \"B) They are adjusted to maximize classification errors\", \"C) They are adjusted to minimize classification errors\", \"D) They are manually set by the network designer\"], \"question\": \"How are connection weights adjusted in a neural network during the training process?\", \"explanation\": \"During training, connection weights are iteratively adjusted through backpropagation to minimize the difference between the network\'s predictions and the actual labels, thereby reducing classification errors.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To detect basic features like edges\", \"B) To combine simple features into complex patterns\", \"C) To convert raw scores into probability distributions for each digit\", \"D) To normalize pixel values in the input layer\"], \"question\": \"What is the specific function of the softmax activation in the output layer of a neural network designed for handwritten digit classification?\", \"explanation\": \"The softmax activation function in the output layer converts the raw output scores (logits) into a probability distribution, where each value represents the probability that the input belongs to a particular digit class, summing to 1.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Multi-layered Perceptron (MLP)\", \"B) Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)\", \"C) LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Network\", \"D) Generative Adversarial Network (GAN)\"], \"question\": \"For a real-time language translation application, which neural network architecture is primarily recommended due to its ability to handle sequential data, variable lengths, and long-term dependencies?\", \"explanation\": \"LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) networks are highly recommended for language translation because LSTMs excel at processing sequential data, handling variable input/output lengths, and maintaining long-term dependencies crucial for accurate translation.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) The use of sigmoid activation in all layers\", \"B) The Rectified Linear Unit (ReLU) activation function\", \"C) Gating mechanisms (forget, input, and output gates)\", \"D) The softmax activation in the output layer\"], \"question\": \"What specific mechanism within Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks helps them solve the vanishing gradient problem and selectively retain or discard information over long sequences?\", \"explanation\": \"LSTM networks utilize specialized gating mechanisms (forget, input, and output gates) to control the flow of information into and out of the cell state, allowing them to selectively remember or forget context over long sequences, thereby mitigating the vanishing gradient problem.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Exploding gradient problem\", \"B) Vanishing gradient problem\", \"C) Overfitting due to too many parameters\", \"D) Insufficient data for training\"], \"question\": \"A student uses the sigmoid activation function in all layers of a deep neural network and observes poor performance. What is the most likely problem they are encountering?\", \"explanation\": \"The sigmoid function\'s derivatives are very small for large positive or negative inputs, leading to gradient saturation. In deep networks, this causes gradients to become progressively smaller as they backpropagate, resulting in the vanishing gradient problem and ineffective weight updates.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}]}', 0, NULL, '2025-12-25 07:42:36'),
(6, 2, 6, NULL, 'asdaf', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Requires extensive manual feature engineering.\", \"B) Struggles with non-linear relationships between variables.\", \"C) Automatically discovers complex patterns without manual feature engineering.\", \"D) Limited to processing only structured data types.\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is a key advantage of deep learning over traditional machine learning for predicting patient readmission risk?\", \"explanation\": \"Deep learning\'s automatic feature learning capability is a significant advantage, as it discovers complex patterns in high-dimensional medical data without the need for manual feature engineering, unlike traditional methods.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Multi-layered Neural Networks to process complex patient data.\", \"B) Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs) for temporal sequences.\", \"C) Natural Language Processing to analyze clinical notes.\", \"D) Simple Linear Regression models for quick baseline predictions.\"], \"question\": \"All of the following are described as application methods of deep learning for patient readmission prediction EXCEPT:\", \"explanation\": \"Simple Linear Regression is a traditional machine learning method, not a deep learning application method described for this scenario. The text explicitly mentions multi-layered NNs, RNNs/LSTMs, and NLP.\", \"correct_answer\": \"D\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To convert raw scores into probability distributions.\", \"B) To receive normalized pixel values as input.\", \"C) To detect basic features like edges, curves, and orientations.\", \"D) To combine simple features into complex patterns like loops and intersections.\"], \"question\": \"In a neural network designed to classify handwritten digits, what is the primary role of the first hidden layer?\", \"explanation\": \"The text states, \'First Hidden Layer: Detects basic features like edges, curves, and orientations.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To determine the activation function used by a neuron.\", \"B) To define the strength of influence between neurons in consecutive layers.\", \"C) To normalize the input pixel values before processing.\", \"D) To convert raw scores into probability distributions in the output layer.\"], \"question\": \"What is the fundamental function of \'connection weights\' in a neural network?\", \"explanation\": \"The text explicitly states, \'Connection Weights: Determine the strength of influence between neurons in consecutive layers.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs).\", \"B) Simple Feedforward Neural Networks.\", \"C) LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Networks.\", \"D) Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs).\"], \"question\": \"For building a real-time language translation application, which neural network architecture is primarily recommended according to the text?\", \"explanation\": \"The text recommends \'LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Networks\' as the primary choice for real-time language translation.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) They process language in parallel, ignoring word order.\", \"B) They require fixed-length input and output sentences.\", \"C) They process language sequentially, maintaining word order and grammatical structure.\", \"D) They are primarily designed for image recognition tasks.\"], \"question\": \"What is a key advantage of LSTM networks for language translation concerning data flow?\", \"explanation\": \"The text states, \'Sequential Processing: LSTMs process language sequentially, maintaining word order and grammatical structure essential for accurate translation.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) By using only very shallow networks to avoid deep dependencies.\", \"B) By ignoring context from early parts of long sentences.\", \"C) By solving the vanishing gradient problem, enabling memory of important context.\", \"D) By converting all sequential data into a single fixed-size vector.\"], \"question\": \"How do LSTM networks address the challenge of \'long-term dependencies\' in sequential data like language?\", \"explanation\": \"The text mentions, \'Long-term Dependencies: LSTMs solve the vanishing gradient problem, enabling the network to remember important context from early parts of long sentences.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Exploding gradient problem.\", \"B) Overfitting due to too many active neurons.\", \"C) Vanishing gradient problem.\", \"D) Inability to handle non-linear relationships.\"], \"question\": \"A student uses the sigmoid activation function in all layers of a deep neural network and observes poor performance. What is the most likely problem they are encountering?\", \"explanation\": \"The text explicitly states, \'The student is experiencing the vanishing gradient problem, which occurs because sigmoid functions have several critical limitations in deep networks.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Their derivatives are always large, causing gradients to explode.\", \"B) Their outputs are always centered around zero, leading to instability.\", \"C) Their derivatives become extremely small for large positive or negative inputs, leading to gradient saturation.\", \"D) They are computationally expensive, slowing down training but not affecting gradients.\"], \"question\": \"Why do sigmoid activation functions contribute to the vanishing gradient problem in deep networks?\", \"explanation\": \"The text explains, \'Gradient Saturation: Sigmoid derivatives range from 0 to 0.25, becoming extremely small for large positive or negative inputs.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Tanh (Hyperbolic Tangent).\", \"B) Softmax.\", \"C) ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit).\", \"D) Linear activation.\"], \"question\": \"Which activation function is recommended as a superior alternative to sigmoid for hidden layers in deep networks, primarily due to its ability to eliminate vanishing gradients and computational efficiency?\", \"explanation\": \"The text recommends \'ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit)\' and lists \'Eliminates Vanishing Gradients\' and \'Computational Efficiency\' as key reasons.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}]}', 0, NULL, '2025-12-25 21:24:28'),
(7, 2, 6, NULL, 'ajdkefgdhbg', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Multi-layered Neural Networks\", \"B) Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs)\", \"C) Natural Language Processing (NLP)\", \"D) Support Vector Machines (SVMs)\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is NOT listed as an application method for deep learning in predicting patient readmission risk?\", \"explanation\": \"The text lists Multi-layered Neural Networks, Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs), Natural Language Processing, and Ensemble Deep Learning as application methods. Support Vector Machines are a traditional machine learning method, not a deep learning application method mentioned here.\", \"correct_answer\": \"D\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Requires extensive manual feature engineering\", \"B) Struggles with non-linear relationships\", \"C) Offers automatic feature learning\", \"D) Performs poorly on large datasets\"], \"question\": \"What is a key advantage of deep learning over traditional machine learning when predicting patient readmission risk, according to the text?\", \"explanation\": \"Deep learning automatically discovers complex patterns and interactions in patient data without requiring manual feature engineering, which is a significant advantage over traditional methods.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To detect basic features like edges\", \"B) To combine simple features into complex patterns\", \"C) To receive pixel values representing grayscale intensities\", \"D) To convert raw scores into probability distributions\"], \"question\": \"In a neural network designed to classify handwritten digits, what is the primary function of the input layer?\", \"explanation\": \"The input layer receives pixel values representing grayscale intensities, with each pixel value serving as a feature.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) They normalize pixel values to a specific range.\", \"B) They determine the strength of influence between neurons in consecutive layers.\", \"C) They convert raw scores into probability distributions for the output.\", \"D) They are fixed values that do not change during training.\"], \"question\": \"What role do connection weights play in a neural network for digit classification?\", \"explanation\": \"Connection weights determine the strength of influence between neurons in consecutive layers and are adjusted during training.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Multi-layered Perceptrons (MLPs)\", \"B) Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)\", \"C) LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Networks\", \"D) Traditional Feedforward Networks\"], \"question\": \"Which type of neural network architecture is primarily recommended for a real-time language translation app, according to the text?\", \"explanation\": \"The text explicitly recommends LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Networks, specifically with Encoder and Decoder LSTMs and an Attention Mechanism, for real-time language translation.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) They prevent overfitting by reducing model complexity.\", \"B) They solve the vanishing gradient problem, enabling the network to remember long-term context.\", \"C) They require less computational power than traditional RNNs for short sentences.\", \"D) They only process sentences in one direction, simplifying memory management.\"], \"question\": \"What is a significant memory handling benefit of LSTMs for language translation?\", \"explanation\": \"LSTMs solve the vanishing gradient problem, which enables the network to remember important context from early parts of long sentences, crucial for maintaining translation coherence.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Exploding gradient problem\", \"B) Dying ReLU problem\", \"C) Vanishing gradient problem\", \"D) Overfitting due to too many parameters\"], \"question\": \"A student uses the sigmoid activation function in all layers of a deep network and observes poor performance. What is the most likely problem they are encountering?\", \"explanation\": \"The text states that using sigmoid functions in deep networks often leads to the vanishing gradient problem because sigmoid derivatives become extremely small, causing gradients to decay exponentially during backpropagation.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) They are computationally expensive to calculate.\", \"B) Their outputs are centered around zero, leading to inefficient optimization.\", \"C) They suffer from gradient saturation, leading to ineffective weight updates.\", \"D) They only allow for sparse activation, reducing network capacity.\"], \"question\": \"Why are sigmoid functions considered problematic for hidden layers in deep neural networks?\", \"explanation\": \"Sigmoid functions suffer from gradient saturation, where their derivatives become very small for large positive or negative inputs, leading to exponential gradient decay and ineffective weight updates in deep networks.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Tanh, because it is computationally more efficient.\", \"B) Leaky ReLU, because it completely eliminates the dying ReLU problem.\", \"C) ReLU, because it eliminates vanishing gradients by not saturating in the positive region.\", \"D) Softmax, because it produces sparse representations.\"], \"question\": \"Which activation function is recommended as a superior alternative to sigmoid for hidden layers in deep networks, and what is its primary advantage?\", \"explanation\": \"ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit) is recommended because it eliminates vanishing gradients; its gradient is 1 for positive inputs, preventing saturation in the positive region and allowing effective gradient flow.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) The input layer receives pixel data.\", \"B) The first hidden layer detects basic features like edges.\", \"C) The output layer uses softmax activation to convert raw scores into probability distributions.\", \"D) Connection weights are adjusted to minimize classification errors.\"], \"question\": \"In a neural network for handwritten digit classification, what is the final step in the forward propagation process after features have been extracted by hidden layers?\", \"explanation\": \"The output layer uses softmax activation to convert raw scores into probability distributions, with the highest probability indicating the predicted digit.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}]}', 0, NULL, '2025-12-26 11:59:04'),
(8, 2, 7, NULL, 'quiz ff', 'hard', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Automatic feature learning from complex patient data.\", \"B) Superior performance on large datasets.\", \"C) Reduced need for extensive computational resources compared to traditional methods.\", \"D) Effective integration of multimodal data like structured records and unstructured notes.\"], \"question\": \"A healthcare startup aims to predict patient readmission risk using deep learning. Which of the following is NOT a direct advantage of deep learning over traditional machine learning for this task?\", \"explanation\": \"Deep learning models often require significant computational resources, especially during training, which is not necessarily an advantage over traditional methods in terms of resource usage. The other options are direct advantages.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Multi-layered Perceptron (MLP)\", \"B) Recurrent Neural Network (RNN) or Long Short-Short Term Memory (LSTM)\", \"C) Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)\", \"D) Autoencoder\"], \"question\": \"When applying deep learning to predict patient readmission, which type of neural network would be most suitable for analyzing the temporal evolution of a patient\'s condition during hospitalization?\", \"explanation\": \"RNNs and LSTMs are specifically designed to handle sequential and temporal data, making them ideal for capturing how patient conditions evolve over time.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To determine the activation function used by the next layer.\", \"B) To encode the network\'s learned knowledge about digit characteristics.\", \"C) To normalize the pixel values of the input image.\", \"D) To define the number of neurons in each hidden layer.\"], \"question\": \"In a neural network designed to classify handwritten digits, what is the primary role of the connection weights between neurons in consecutive layers?\", \"explanation\": \"Connection weights determine the strength of influence between neurons and are adjusted during training to encode the network\'s learned knowledge, allowing it to recognize patterns.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) By directly mapping pixel values to digit probabilities in the input layer.\", \"B) Through hierarchical feature extraction, where each layer builds increasingly abstract representations.\", \"C) By using a single activation function across all layers to identify the digit.\", \"D) By randomly assigning probabilities to digits based on input intensity.\"], \"question\": \"During the forward propagation process in a digit classification neural network, how does the network transform low-level pixel data into a final classification?\", \"explanation\": \"The network processes input through multiple layers, with each layer extracting and combining features to build more abstract representations, ultimately leading to a classification.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) They use a simpler activation function that prevents gradient issues.\", \"B) They solve the vanishing gradient problem, enabling the network to remember context from early parts of long sentences.\", \"C) They process all words simultaneously, making them faster for long sequences.\", \"D) They only consider the last few words of a sentence, simplifying the translation process.\"], \"question\": \"For a real-time language translation application, an LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) network is recommended. What is a key advantage of LSTMs in handling long sentences for translation?\", \"explanation\": \"LSTMs are designed with gating mechanisms that help them overcome the vanishing gradient problem, allowing them to maintain and utilize long-term dependencies and context across extended sequences.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Encoder LSTM\", \"B) Decoder LSTM\", \"C) Attention Mechanism\", \"D) Cell State\"], \"question\": \"Which component of an LSTM-based Seq2Seq network is responsible for focusing on relevant parts of the input sentence during the translation process?\", \"explanation\": \"The attention mechanism allows the decoder to focus on specific parts of the input sentence that are most relevant for generating the current output word, improving translation quality.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Overfitting due to too many parameters.\", \"B) The vanishing gradient problem, leading to slow or stalled learning in early layers.\", \"C) Exploding gradients, causing unstable training.\", \"D) Insufficient data for training the deep network.\"], \"question\": \"A student uses the sigmoid activation function in all layers of a deep network and observes poor performance. What is the most likely problem they are encountering?\", \"explanation\": \"Sigmoid functions are prone to gradient saturation, where derivatives become very small, leading to the vanishing gradient problem as gradients backpropagate through deep networks, hindering learning.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) ReLU is computationally more complex but provides higher accuracy.\", \"B) ReLU eliminates the vanishing gradient problem for positive inputs and is computationally efficient.\", \"C) ReLU outputs are always centered around zero, which speeds up convergence.\", \"D) ReLU is only suitable for binary classification tasks, unlike sigmoid.\"], \"question\": \"Why is ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit) generally preferred over sigmoid for hidden layers in deep neural networks?\", \"explanation\": \"ReLU\'s gradient is 1 for positive inputs, preventing vanishing gradients in that region, and its simple thresholding operation makes it computationally very efficient compared to sigmoid.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Its output is always positive.\", \"B) Its derivative is always 1.\", \"C) Its derivatives become extremely small for large positive or negative inputs (gradient saturation).\", \"D) It requires more computational power than other activation functions.\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is a disadvantage of sigmoid activation functions that contributes to the vanishing gradient problem?\", \"explanation\": \"The sigmoid function\'s derivatives approach zero for large positive or negative inputs, causing gradient saturation and leading to vanishing gradients during backpropagation.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Transformers are unable to handle variable-length sentences.\", \"B) LSTMs have lower computational requirements and memory efficiency, making them better suited for mobile deployment.\", \"C) LSTMs can process sentences bidirectionally, while Transformers cannot.\", \"D) Transformers are prone to the vanishing gradient problem, unlike LSTMs.\"], \"question\": \"While Transformer architectures offer superior performance for language translation, why might LSTM-based Seq2Seq networks still be preferable for real-time mobile applications?\", \"explanation\": \"Transformers are generally more computationally intensive. LSTMs, while potentially less accurate than state-of-the-art Transformers, offer a better balance of performance and efficiency for resource-constrained environments like mobile devices.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}]}', 0, NULL, '2026-01-04 09:25:40'),
(9, 2, 6, 6, 'Quiz first', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Multi-layered Neural Networks for processing complex patient data.\", \"B) Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs) for handling temporal sequences.\", \"C) Natural Language Processing (NLP) for analyzing unstructured clinical notes.\", \"D) Decision Trees for automatic feature learning and pattern identification.\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is NOT a method for applying deep learning to predict patient readmission risk, as described in the text?\", \"explanation\": \"The text lists Multi-layered Neural Networks, RNNs/LSTMs, and Natural Language Processing as deep learning application methods. Decision Trees are a traditional machine learning algorithm, not a deep learning method mentioned in this context.\", \"correct_answer\": \"D\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) It requires extensive manual feature engineering for high-dimensional medical data.\", \"B) It struggles to model non-linear relationships between multiple variables.\", \"C) It automatically discovers complex patterns and interactions without requiring manual feature engineering.\", \"D) It typically achieves lower accuracy compared to traditional methods when sufficient data is available.\"], \"question\": \"What is a key advantage of deep learning over traditional machine learning in the context of patient readmission prediction?\", \"explanation\": \"The text states that deep learning \'automatically discovers complex patterns and interactions in patient data without requiring manual feature engineering,\' which is a significant advantage.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To detect basic features like edges and curves.\", \"B) To combine simple features into complex patterns.\", \"C) To receive pixel values representing grayscale intensities.\", \"D) To convert raw scores into probability distributions for digits.\"], \"question\": \"In a neural network designed to classify handwritten digits, what is the primary role of the input layer?\", \"explanation\": \"The input layer receives pixel values representing grayscale intensities, with each pixel value serving as a feature.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To output the final classification probabilities.\", \"B) To receive raw pixel data from the image.\", \"C) To detect basic features like edges, curves, and orientations.\", \"D) To adjust connection weights during the learning process.\"], \"question\": \"What is the specific function of the first hidden layer in a neural network for handwritten digit classification?\", \"explanation\": \"The text specifies that the \'First Hidden Layer: Detects basic features like edges, curves, and orientations.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) It performs edge detection on raw pixel data.\", \"B) It combines simple features into complex patterns.\", \"C) It uses softmax activation to convert raw scores into probability distributions for digits.\", \"D) It adjusts weights to minimize classification errors.\"], \"question\": \"How does the output layer function in a neural network for handwritten digit classification?\", \"explanation\": \"The output layer uses \'softmax activation to convert raw scores into probability distributions\' where the highest probability indicates the predicted digit.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Standard Feedforward Neural Network.\", \"B) Convolutional Neural Network (CNN).\", \"C) LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Networks.\", \"D) Autoencoder.\"], \"question\": \"For a real-time language translation application, which neural network architecture is primarily recommended according to the text?\", \"explanation\": \"The text explicitly recommends \'LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Networks\' as the primary architecture for a real-time language translation app.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) They struggle with variable-length sentences, requiring fixed input sizes.\", \"B) They are prone to the vanishing gradient problem in long sequences, losing context.\", \"C) Gating mechanisms allow them to selectively retain or discard information, maintaining coherence.\", \"D) They require extensive manual feature engineering to preserve semantic meaning.\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is a key memory handling benefit of LSTMs for language translation?\", \"explanation\": \"The text highlights that \'Gating mechanisms (forget, input, output gates) allow the network to selectively retain or discard information, crucial for maintaining translation coherence.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Exploding gradient problem.\", \"B) Overfitting due to ReLU\'s linearity.\", \"C) Vanishing gradient problem.\", \"D) Too much computational efficiency leading to underfitting.\"], \"question\": \"A student uses the sigmoid activation function in all layers of a deep network and notices poor performance. What is the most likely problem they are encountering?\", \"explanation\": \"The text states that using sigmoid functions in deep networks leads to the \'vanishing gradient problem\' due to their critical limitations.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) It causes gradient saturation, leading to slow learning in deeper layers.\", \"B) Its non-zero centered outputs lead to inefficient optimization.\", \"C) It eliminates vanishing gradients and is computationally efficient.\", \"D) It requires complex exponential calculations, increasing training time significantly.\"], \"question\": \"Why is ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit) considered a superior alternative to sigmoid for hidden layers in deep networks?\", \"explanation\": \"The text explains that ReLU \'Eliminates Vanishing Gradients\' and offers \'Computational Efficiency\' due to its simple thresholding operation.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) They always produce outputs centered around zero.\", \"B) Their derivatives become extremely small for large positive or negative inputs.\", \"C) They have a constant gradient of 1 for all positive inputs.\", \"D) They are computationally more efficient than ReLU.\"], \"question\": \"Which characteristic of sigmoid functions primarily contributes to the vanishing gradient problem in deep networks?\", \"explanation\": \"The text states that \'Sigmoid derivatives range from to becoming extremely small for large positive or negative inputs,\' which leads to exponential gradient decay and the vanishing gradient problem.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}]}', 1, '2026-01-05 13:42:14', '2026-01-05 19:12:00'),
(10, 2, 5, 6, 'First Quiz', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Apply AI technologies to develop comprehensive marketing strategies for new product development\", \"B) Utilize no-code AI platforms to analyze competitor products and identify market opportunities\", \"C) Develop advanced AI algorithms from scratch for marketing research\", \"D) Implement ethical AI frameworks in marketing research and customer targeting\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is NOT a primary learning objective of the AI-Powered Competitive Product Strategy and Market Entry Plan project?\", \"explanation\": \"The project focuses on applying existing AI technologies and utilizing no-code platforms, not developing advanced AI algorithms from scratch.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) New Product Concept Development\", \"B) Customer Journey Mapping and Persona Development\", \"C) Strategic Marketing Mix (4Ps) with AI Integration\", \"D) Marketing Technology Implementation Plan\"], \"question\": \"In Phase AI-Driven Market Research and Competitive Analysis, what is a key deliverable related to customer understanding?\", \"explanation\": \"Deliverable 1B specifically covers Customer Journey Mapping and Persona Development, which is crucial for understanding customers.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Predictive modeling\", \"B) Sentiment analysis\", \"C) Image recognition\", \"D) Natural Language Generation\"], \"question\": \"Which AI tool application is explicitly mentioned for analyzing customer reviews, ratings, and feedback patterns in Deliverable 1A?\", \"explanation\": \"Deliverable 1A states: \'Analyze customer reviews, ratings, and feedback patterns using sentiment analysis\'.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Competitor\'s existing product features\", \"B) AI-driven feature prioritization based on customer needs analysis\", \"C) Internal team\'s subjective preferences\", \"D) Budget constraints only\"], \"question\": \"When developing a new product concept in Phase AI-Enhanced Product Development and Brand Strategy, what is used for feature prioritization?\", \"explanation\": \"Deliverable 2A specifies: \'AI-driven feature prioritization based on customer needs analysis\'.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Product Strategy\", \"B) Pricing Strategy\", \"C) Promotion Strategy\", \"D) Place Strategy\"], \"question\": \"Which aspect of the marketing mix (4Ps) involves \'Digital distribution channel optimization\' and \'Omnichannel customer experience design\' in Phase AI-Powered Marketing Mix Optimization?\", \"explanation\": \"Digital distribution channel optimization and Omnichannel customer experience design fall under the \'Place Strategy\' in Deliverable 3A.\", \"correct_answer\": \"D\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Ensuring all marketing content is positive\", \"B) Preventing bias in AI-driven targeting and personalization\", \"C) Avoiding any use of AI in marketing\", \"D) Only targeting high-income customers\"], \"question\": \"What is a key consideration for \'Bias prevention\' in the Ethical AI Marketing Framework (Deliverable 4B)?\", \"explanation\": \"Deliverable 4B explicitly states: \'Bias prevention in AI-driven targeting and personalization\' as a requirement.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Deliverable 2A: New Product Concept Development\", \"B) Deliverable 3A: Strategic Marketing Mix (4Ps) with AI Integration\", \"C) Deliverable 1A: Product Selection and Competitive Intelligence Report\", \"D) Deliverable 4A: Marketing Technology Implementation Plan\"], \"question\": \"Which deliverable requires the creation of an \'AI-driven content marketing calendar\' and \'Social media automation and engagement strategy\'?\", \"explanation\": \"The \'Promotion Strategy\' section within Deliverable 3A includes \'AI-driven content marketing calendar\' and \'Social media automation and engagement strategy\'.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To replicate the product exactly\", \"B) To develop a comprehensive AI-powered strategy to launch a competing product\", \"C) To analyze the product\'s manufacturing process\", \"D) To interview the original product\'s creator\"], \"question\": \"The project requires students to select ONE existing successful product from an online shopping platform. What is the subsequent task related to this selection?\", \"explanation\": \"The project context states: \'Your task is to select an existing successful product... and develop comprehensive AI-powered strategy to launch competing product\'.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) 02_Product_Brand_Strategy/\", \"B) 01_Market_Research/\", \"C) 03_Marketing_Mix_Strategy/\", \"D) 04_Implementation_Ethics/\"], \"question\": \"In the Digital Portfolio Structure, where would you find the \'competitive_analysis_report.pdf\'?\", \"explanation\": \"The \'competitive_analysis_report.pdf\' is listed under the \'01_Market_Research/\' folder in the submission requirements.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) marketing_mix_optimization_plan.pdf\", \"B) strategy_summary_video.mp4\", \"C) budget_roi_calculator.xlsx\", \"D) customer_journey_map.pdf\"], \"question\": \"What is an optional submission requirement for the \'06_Executive_Presentation/\' folder?\", \"explanation\": \"The \'strategy_summary_video.mp4 (Optional Max minutes)\' is listed under the \'06_Executive_Presentation/\' folder.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}]}', 1, '2026-01-05 14:26:21', '2026-01-05 19:53:05');
INSERT INTO `ai_quizzes` (`id`, `user_id`, `resource_id`, `subject_id`, `title`, `difficulty`, `num_questions`, `quiz_data`, `is_published`, `published_at`, `created_at`) VALUES
(11, 2, 5, 6, 'quizz', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Apply AI technologies to develop comprehensive marketing strategies for new product development\", \"B) Utilize no-code AI platforms to analyze competitor products and identify market opportunities\", \"C) Develop advanced AI algorithms from scratch for marketing research\", \"D) Implement ethical AI frameworks in marketing research and customer targeting\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is NOT a primary learning objective for the AI-Powered Competitive Product Strategy and Market Entry Plan project?\", \"explanation\": \"The project focuses on applying AI technologies and utilizing no-code platforms, not on developing advanced AI algorithms from scratch.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) New Product Concept Development\", \"B) Customer Journey Mapping and Persona Development\", \"C) Strategic Marketing Mix (4Ps) with AI Integration\", \"D) Marketing Technology Implementation Plan\"], \"question\": \"In Phase AI-Driven Market Research and Competitive Analysis, what is a key deliverable related to customer understanding?\", \"explanation\": \"Deliverable 1B specifically covers Customer Journey Mapping and Persona Development, which is crucial for understanding customers.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Predictive modeling\", \"B) Sentiment analysis\", \"C) Image recognition\", \"D) Natural Language Generation\"], \"question\": \"Which AI tool application is explicitly mentioned for analyzing customer reviews, ratings, and feedback patterns in Deliverable 1A?\", \"explanation\": \"Deliverable 1A states: \'Analyze customer reviews, ratings, and feedback patterns using sentiment analysis\'.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Expert opinion only\", \"B) Random selection\", \"C) AI-driven feature prioritization based on customer needs analysis\", \"D) Competitor feature replication\"], \"question\": \"When developing a new product concept in Phase AI-Enhanced Product Development and Brand Strategy, what AI-driven approach is suggested for feature prioritization?\", \"explanation\": \"Deliverable 2A specifies \'AI-driven feature prioritization based on customer needs analysis\' for new product concept development.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Value-based pricing optimization\", \"B) Digital distribution channel optimization\", \"C) AI-driven content marketing calendar\", \"D) Service design using AI insights\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is a component of the \'Promotion Strategy\' within the AI-Powered Marketing Mix Optimization phase?\", \"explanation\": \"The \'Promotion Strategy\' section in Deliverable 3A includes \'AI-driven content marketing calendar\'.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) AI-enhanced product development roadmap\", \"B) Revenue model innovation using AI insights\", \"C) Omnichannel customer experience design\", \"D) Personal selling enhancement using AI tools\"], \"question\": \"What is a key aspect of the \'Place Strategy\' in the AI-Powered Marketing Mix Optimization phase?\", \"explanation\": \"The \'Place Strategy\' section in Deliverable 3A includes \'Omnichannel customer experience design\'.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Budget allocation for AI marketing tools\", \"B) Bias prevention\", \"C) KPI framework definition\", \"D) Team structure and skill requirements\"], \"question\": \"In the \'Implementation Roadmap and Ethical Framework\' phase, what is a crucial ethical consideration students must address regarding AI-driven targeting and personalization?\", \"explanation\": \"Deliverable 4B, \'Ethical AI Marketing Framework\', explicitly lists \'Bias prevention in AI-driven targeting and personalization\'.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) .pdf\", \"B) .xlsx\", \"C) .mp4\", \"D) .txt\"], \"question\": \"Which file format is suggested for the \'strategy_summary_video\' in the submission requirements?\", \"explanation\": \"The submission requirements list \'strategy_summary_video.mp4\' as an optional deliverable.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To optimize pricing strategies\", \"B) To develop brand identity\", \"C) To analyze market gaps\", \"D) To map customer journeys\"], \"question\": \"What is the purpose of \'AI-assisted creative elements\' in Deliverable 2A?\", \"explanation\": \"Deliverable 2A states \'Brand identity development with AI-assisted creative elements\'.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To develop new AI algorithms for marketing\", \"B) To challenge an established product in the online marketplace\", \"C) To manage an existing product\'s marketing campaigns\", \"D) To conduct academic research on AI ethics only\"], \"question\": \"According to the project context, what is the student\'s role as a Marketing Strategy Consultant?\", \"explanation\": \"The \'Business Scenario\' states: \'You are Marketing Strategy Consultant hired by an emerging startup to challenge an established product in the online marketplace.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}]}', 1, '2026-01-05 14:46:00', '2026-01-05 20:15:39'),
(12, 2, 6, 4, 'quizez', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Multi-layered Neural Networks to process complex patient data.\", \"B) Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs/LSTMs) to handle temporal sequences of patient data.\", \"C) Natural Language Processing to analyze unstructured clinical notes.\", \"D) Support Vector Machines (SVMs) for feature extraction and classification.\"], \"question\": \"A healthcare startup wants to predict patient readmission risk using historical data. Which of the following is NOT a deep learning application method mentioned for this scenario?\", \"explanation\": \"The text lists Multi-layered Neural Networks, RNNs/LSTMs, and Natural Language Processing as deep learning application methods for patient readmission prediction. Support Vector Machines (SVMs) are a traditional machine learning algorithm, not a deep learning method.\", \"correct_answer\": \"D\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) It requires extensive manual feature engineering, which improves model interpretability.\", \"B) It struggles to capture non-linear relationships between multiple variables.\", \"C) It automatically discovers complex patterns and interactions in patient data without requiring manual feature engineering.\", \"D) It performs best on small, highly structured datasets, limiting its use in healthcare.\"], \"question\": \"What is a significant advantage of deep learning over traditional machine learning for predicting patient readmission risk, as described in the provided text?\", \"explanation\": \"The text states \'Automatic Feature Learning: Deep learning automatically discovers complex patterns and interactions in patient data without requiring manual feature engineering,\' which is a key advantage.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) It performs complex mathematical transformations to generate new features.\", \"B) It receives pixel values representing grayscale intensities, normalized to a range like 0-1.\", \"C) It converts pixel data into audio signals for processing by subsequent layers.\", \"D) It directly outputs the predicted digit based on raw pixel values.\"], \"question\": \"In a neural network designed to classify handwritten digits, how does the input layer typically process pixel data?\", \"explanation\": \"The text explains: \'Input layer receives neurons pixel values) representing grayscale intensities normalized to Each pixel value serves as feature representing local image characteristics.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To determine the color scheme of the output image.\", \"B) To define the strength of influence between neurons in consecutive layers.\", \"C) To randomly assign initial values to neurons without further adjustment.\", \"D) To control the network\'s overall computational power.\"], \"question\": \"What is the primary role of \'connection weights\' in a neural network, as described in the context of digit classification?\", \"explanation\": \"The text states: \'Connection Weights: Determine the strength of influence between neurons in consecutive layers.\' These weights are adjusted during training.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) due to their efficiency in processing image data.\", \"B) Feedforward Neural Networks (FNNs) for their simplicity and speed.\", \"C) LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Networks for their ability to handle sequential data and long-term dependencies.\", \"D) Autoencoders for their effectiveness in data compression and dimensionality reduction.\"], \"question\": \"For a real-time language translation application, which neural network architecture is primarily recommended in the text, and why?\", \"explanation\": \"The text recommends \'LSTM-based Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Networks\' due to their advantages in sequential processing, variable length handling, and memory handling for long-term dependencies, which are crucial for language translation.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) The exclusive use of sigmoid activation functions in all layers.\", \"B) Gating mechanisms (forget, input, output gates) and a cell state that selectively retains or discards information.\", \"C) A fixed number of hidden layers that prevent gradients from decaying.\", \"D) Randomly initialized weights that are never updated during training.\"], \"question\": \"What specific mechanism within LSTMs allows them to solve the vanishing gradient problem and maintain long-term dependencies, crucial for tasks like language translation?\", \"explanation\": \"The text explains that \'LSTMs solve the vanishing gradient problem\' and mentions \'Gating mechanisms (forget, input, output gates) allow the network to selectively retain or discard information\' and \'Cell state maintains semantic meaning across the entire translation process.\'\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Exploding gradient problem, where gradients become too large.\", \"B) Vanishing gradient problem, where gradients become extremely small.\", \"C) Overfitting due to too few parameters in the network.\", \"D) Underfitting due to an excessively complex model architecture.\"], \"question\": \"A student uses the sigmoid activation function in all layers of a deep network and observes poor performance. What is the most likely problem they are encountering?\", \"explanation\": \"The text explicitly states: \'The student is experiencing the vanishing gradient problem, which occurs because sigmoid functions have several critical limitations in deep networks,\' such as gradient saturation and exponential gradient decay.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Tanh, because it has a wider output range than sigmoid.\", \"B) Softmax, because it is ideal for binary classification tasks.\", \"C) ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit), because it eliminates vanishing gradients in the positive region and is computationally efficient.\", \"D) Linear activation, because it simplifies the network\'s learning process.\"], \"question\": \"What activation function is recommended as a superior alternative to sigmoid for hidden layers in deep networks, and why?\", \"explanation\": \"The text recommends \'ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit)\' and explains its superiority by stating it \'Eliminates Vanishing Gradients\' (no saturation in the positive region) and offers \'Computational Efficiency\' (simple thresholding operation).\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Its output is always centered around zero, which slows down optimization.\", \"B) Its derivatives become extremely small for large positive or negative inputs, leading to gradient saturation.\", \"C) It only works with positive input values, limiting its applicability.\", \"D) It requires more complex exponential calculations than other activation functions, increasing training time.\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is a key limitation of the sigmoid activation function that contributes to the vanishing gradient problem in deep neural networks?\", \"explanation\": \"The text states: \'Gradient Saturation: Sigmoid derivatives range from to becoming extremely small for large positive or negative inputs,\' which causes exponential gradient decay and the vanishing gradient problem.\", \"correct_answer\": \"B\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) It always outputs values between 0 and 1, similar to probabilities.\", \"B) It has a non-zero centered output, which aids in more efficient optimization.\", \"C) It prevents gradient saturation in the positive region, allowing for better gradient flow and effective training of deep networks.\", \"D) It requires more complex computations than sigmoid, leading to more robust models.\"], \"question\": \"Which characteristic primarily makes ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit) a preferred activation function over sigmoid for hidden layers in deep networks?\", \"explanation\": \"The text highlights that ReLU \'Eliminates Vanishing Gradients\' because it has a gradient of 1 for positive inputs, meaning \'No saturation in positive region prevents gradient decay,\' which enables effective training of very deep networks.\", \"correct_answer\": \"C\"}]}', 1, '2026-01-05 14:48:33', '2026-01-05 20:18:21'),
(13, 2, 10, 4, 'timeseries quiz 1', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Mean, variance, and autocorrelation\", \"B) Trend, seasonality, and residuals\", \"C) Only the mean and trend\", \"D) Only the variance and seasonality\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following properties must remain constant over time for a time series to be considered stationary?\", \"explanation\": \"Stationarity in a time series means that its statistical properties like mean, variance, and autocorrelation do not change over time. This is crucial for many forecasting models.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Integrated; to make the series stationary through differencing\", \"B) Independent; to ensure observations are not correlated\", \"C) Iterative; to refine model parameters repeatedly\", \"D) Influential; to identify key data points\"], \"question\": \"What does the \'I\' in ARIMA stand for, and what is its purpose?\", \"explanation\": \"In ARIMA, \'I\' stands for Integrated, which refers to the differencing of raw observations to make the time series stationary. This step removes trends and seasonality.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) It gradually decreases\", \"B) It cuts off sharply after a few lags\", \"C) It shows no significant correlation\", \"D) It oscillates randomly\"], \"question\": \"How does the Autocorrelation Function (ACF) typically behave for an AR (Auto-Regressive) model?\", \"explanation\": \"For AR models, the ACF (Autocorrelation Function) gradually decreases, indicating a decaying correlation with increasing lags. This helps in identifying the order of MA models, while PACF helps for AR models.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To smooth out short-term fluctuations and highlight long-term trends\", \"B) To identify the order of AR models\", \"C) To measure the correlation between a series and its past values\", \"D) To decompose a series into trend, seasonality, and residuals\"], \"question\": \"What is the primary purpose of a Moving Average (MA) in time series analysis?\", \"explanation\": \"Moving Average is a statistical method used to smooth out short-term fluctuations and highlight long-term trends or patterns in time series data by averaging data points over a fixed number of periods.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Trend, Seasonality, and Residual\", \"B) Mean, Variance, and Autocorrelation\", \"C) AR, I, and MA components\", \"D) Observed, Forecasted, and Error\"], \"question\": \"A time series decomposition typically breaks down the original series into which three components?\", \"explanation\": \"Time series can be decomposed into Trend (long-term increase or decrease), Seasonality (repeating short-term cycle), and Residual (random noise). So, Time Series = Trend + Seasonality + Residual.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Seasonal components (P, D, Q) and length of seasonality (s)\", \"B) White noise and stationarity tests\", \"C) Exponential smoothing factors\", \"D) Partial autocorrelation functions\"], \"question\": \"What additional components does SARIMA introduce compared to ARIMA?\", \"explanation\": \"SARIMA (Seasonal Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average) is an extension of ARIMA that adds seasonal components (P, D, Q) and the length of seasonality (s) to account for both trend and seasonality in the data.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) More weight is given to recent observations\", \"B) More weight is given to older observations\", \"C) The forecast will be smoother and less responsive\", \"D) The model is less prone to overfitting\"], \"question\": \"In Exponential Smoothing, what does a higher smoothing factor (alpha) imply?\", \"explanation\": \"In Exponential Smoothing, a higher smoothing factor (alpha) gives more weight to recent observations, making the forecast more responsive to recent changes in the data.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) It exhibits a clear trend or seasonality\", \"B) Values are completely uncorrelated\", \"C) It has a constant mean\", \"D) It has a constant variance\"], \"question\": \"Which characteristic is NOT typical of a White Noise time series?\", \"explanation\": \"White Noise is a random time series where values are completely uncorrelated, with constant mean and variance. It explicitly does NOT have any trend or seasonality.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To make a non-stationary series stationary\", \"B) To introduce seasonality into the data\", \"C) To increase the variance of the series\", \"D) To smooth out random fluctuations\"], \"question\": \"What is the primary goal of differencing a time series?\", \"explanation\": \"Differencing is a technique used to transform a non-stationary time series (one with a trend or changing mean) into a stationary one, which is a requirement for many forecasting methods like ARIMA.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Yt - Yt-1\", \"B) Yt - Yt-2\", \"C) (Yt - Yt-1) - (Yt-1 - Yt-2)\", \"D) Yt / Yt-1\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following is an example of first-order differencing?\", \"explanation\": \"First-order differencing involves subtracting the value of the series at the previous time step from the current value, represented as Yt - Yt-1. This helps remove trends.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}]}', 1, '2026-01-06 01:24:39', '2026-01-06 06:54:09'),
(14, 2, 10, 4, '1', 'medium', 10, '{\"questions\": [{\"options\": [\"A) Mean, variance, and autocorrelation\", \"B) Trend, seasonality, and residuals\", \"C) Only the mean\", \"D) Only the variance\"], \"question\": \"Which of the following properties must remain constant over time for a time series to be considered stationary?\", \"explanation\": \"Stationarity in a time series means that its statistical properties like mean, variance, and autocorrelation do not change over time. This is crucial for many forecasting models.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Integrated; Differencing of raw observations to make the series stationary\", \"B) Independent; Ensuring observations are not correlated\", \"C) Iterative; Repeating the model fitting process multiple times\", \"D) Important; Highlighting the significance of the model\"], \"question\": \"What does the \'I\' in ARIMA stand for, and what is its purpose?\", \"explanation\": \"In ARIMA, \'I\' stands for Integrated, which refers to the differencing of raw observations to make the time series stationary, a necessary step for many models.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Autocorrelation Function (ACF)\", \"B) Partial Autocorrelation Function (PACF)\", \"C) Cross-Correlation Function (CCF)\", \"D) Impulse Response Function (IRF)\"], \"question\": \"Which function is primarily used to identify the order of MA (Moving Average) models and detect seasonality?\", \"explanation\": \"ACF (Autocorrelation Function) measures the correlation of a time series with its own past values (lags) and is useful in identifying seasonality and the order of MA models.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To measure the correlation between a series and its lag after removing the effects of intermediate lags, helping identify AR model order.\", \"B) To smooth out short-term fluctuations in the data.\", \"C) To decompose a time series into trend, seasonality, and residuals.\", \"D) To determine if a time series is white noise.\"], \"question\": \"What is the primary purpose of the Partial Autocorrelation Function (PACF)?\", \"explanation\": \"PACF (Partial Autocorrelation Function) measures the correlation between a series and its lag, after removing the effects of intermediate lags, and is primarily used to identify the order of AR models.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To smooth out short-term fluctuations and highlight long-term trends or patterns.\", \"B) To identify the order of autoregressive components.\", \"C) To remove seasonality from the data.\", \"D) To forecast future values by giving more weight to recent observations.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main goal of using a Moving Average (MA) in time series analysis?\", \"explanation\": \"Moving Average (MA) is a statistical method used to smooth out short-term fluctuations and highlight long-term trends or patterns in time series data.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Random variations in the data after removing trend and seasonality.\", \"B) The long-term increase or decrease in the series.\", \"C) Repeating short-term cycles within the data.\", \"D) The original observed time series.\"], \"question\": \"In time series decomposition, what does the \'Residual\' component represent?\", \"explanation\": \"The Residual component in time series decomposition represents the irregular part of the data, which consists of random variations that do not follow a fixed pattern, after removing trend and seasonality.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Seasonal components (P, D, S) to account for seasonality.\", \"B) Exponential smoothing factors.\", \"C) White noise parameters.\", \"D) Differencing for stationarity only.\"], \"question\": \"What additional components does SARIMA add to the ARIMA model?\", \"explanation\": \"SARIMA (Seasonal Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average) is an extension of the ARIMA model that adds seasonal components (P, D, S) to handle data showing both trend and seasonality.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) All types of exponential smoothing inherently give more weight to recent observations.\", \"B) Simple Moving Average (SMA)\", \"C) Only Holt-Winters (Triple Exponential Smoothing)\", \"D) Only when the smoothing factor is low.\"], \"question\": \"Which type of exponential smoothing gives more weight to recent observations?\", \"explanation\": \"Exponential smoothing forecasts future values by giving more weight to recent observations while still considering older ones. This is a fundamental characteristic of exponential smoothing methods.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) Values are completely uncorrelated, with constant mean and variance, and no trend or seasonality.\", \"B) It exhibits a clear upward or downward trend.\", \"C) It has repeating seasonal patterns.\", \"D) Its autocorrelation function shows significant spikes at various lags.\"], \"question\": \"What are the characteristics of a White Noise time series?\", \"explanation\": \"White Noise is a random time series where values are completely uncorrelated, with constant mean and variance, and no trend or seasonality. Its ACF shows no significant correlation.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}, {\"options\": [\"A) To turn a non-stationary time series into a stationary one by subtracting past values.\", \"B) To smooth out short-term fluctuations in the data.\", \"C) To identify the order of MA models.\", \"D) To forecast future values by giving more weight to recent observations.\"], \"question\": \"What is the primary purpose of differencing in time series analysis?\", \"explanation\": \"Differencing is a technique used to turn a non-stationary time series (one with a trend or changing mean) into a stationary one by subtracting past values, which is required by many forecasting methods like ARIMA.\", \"correct_answer\": \"A\"}]}', 1, '2026-01-06 03:28:18', '2026-01-06 08:57:57');

